            {
              "title": "Fagerström Test for Nicotine Dependence",
              "description": "We used the Fagerstrom Test for Nicotine Dependence (FTND) to measure nicotine dependence.\n\nThe measure consists of 6 Questions. Each question has multiple response options out of which one option must be selected. Each option carries a corresponding numerical score. The scores for each question are summed to obtain a total score. The range of possible scores is 1 to 10, with a higher value indicating greater nicotine dependence (worse outcome).\n\nThe interpretation of scores is as follows:\n\n1-2: low dependence 3-4: low to moderate dependence 5-7: moderate dependence 8+: high dependence",
              "paramType": "MEAN",
              "dispersionType": "STANDARD_DEVIATION",
              "unitOfMeasure": "score",
              "classes": [
                {
                  "categories": [
