            {
              "title": "Programmed Cell Death Ligand 1 (PD-L1) Status at Baseline",
              "description": "Participants were assessed for their PD-L1 tumor expression level by immunohistochemistry assay using tumor tissue from a biopsy. Randomization of participants in the study was stratified by PD-L1 tumor proportion score (TPS) at baseline (\\<1%, 1-49%, or ≥ 50%). Higher percentages of PD-L1 TPS staining correspond to higher positivity of PD-L1 on a tumor. Participants were classified as follows: \\<1% = PD-L1 negative, 1-49% = PD-L1 weakly positive; and ≥50% = PD-L1 strongly positive.",
