              "type": "ACTIVE_COMPARATOR",
              "description": "subjects on the +EIASD treatment arm were taking one of these antiseizure drugs: phenytoin, carbamazepine, phenobarbital, primidone and oxcarbazepine.\n\nSubjects will take terameprocol for 5 consecutive days each month by IV. Starting dose is 750mg/day. Dose escalation is 750, 1100, 1700, 2200, 3000, 4000, 5300, 7000, and 9300. NO intrasubject dose escalation.\n\nPK (pharmacological study) data will be collected on day one of cycle one infusion",
              "interventionNames": [
                "Drug: terameprocol",
                "Other: pharmacological study"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "With Non enzyme-inducing antiseizure drugs (-EIASD)",
              "type": "ACTIVE_COMPARATOR",
              "description": "Subjects in the -EIASD group were either not being treated with antiseizure drugs or were taking ones that did not significantly induce hepatic enzymes such as gabapentin, lamotrigine, valproic acid, levetiracetam, tiagabine, topiramate, zonisamide and felbamate.\n\nSubjects will take terameprocol for 5 consecutive days each month by IV. Starting dose is 750mg/day. Dose escalation is 750, 1100, 1700, 2200, 3000, 4000, 5300, 7000, and 9300. NO intrasubject dose escalation.\n\nPK (pharmacological study) data will be collected on day one of cycle one infusion",
